## Automatic Invariant Verification

Every time a value is mutated, all invariants are re-checked:

```xiom
pub type PositiveInt = Int
  invariant: this > 0;

fn main() -> Int {
  var x: PositiveInt = 5;    // Invariant checked ✓
  x = 10;                     // Invariant checked ✓
  x = x - 5;                  // Invariant checked ✓ (5 > 0)
  // x = x - 10;              // Would VIOLATE: -5 > 0 is false
  return x;
}
```

### Mutation Through Methods

```xiom
pub type SafeStack = {
  data: Vec[Int];
} invariant: self.data.len() <= 1000;

impl SafeStack {
  fn push(self: &mut Self, item: Int)
    requires: self.data.len() < 1000;
  {
    self.data.push(item);  // Invariant re-checked after push ✓
  }

  fn pop(self: &mut Self) -> Int
    requires: self.data.len() > 0;
  {
    return self.data.pop();  // Invariant re-checked ✓
  }
}
```

### Partial Update Safety

```xiom
pub type Rectangle = {
  width: Float64;
  height: Float64;
} invariant: this.width > 0.0 && this.height > 0.0;

fn main() {
  var rect = Rectangle{ width: 10.0, height: 5.0 };
  rect.width = 20.0;   // Invariant re-checked ✓
  rect.width = -1.0;   // VIOLATION! width must be > 0
}
```

### The Timing
Invariant checks happen:
1. After construction (let x: Type = ...)
2. After each field assignment
3. After each method call that takes &mut self
4. After pattern match reassignment

This means you literally CANNOT create or hold an invalid value of an invariant-protected type.

